  "description": "#191: `receiver_session_id` names the one session allowed to register a restore. The response reports the DERIVED controller id (uuid5 of the session id, the same derivation /status reports as `agent_id`), never the session id itself. It is UUID-shaped, so `preserve_identity` keeps it verbatim -- without it, a receiver of B and a receiver of A would normalize to the same `<UUID>`.",
